<title>FINLAND: Swedish pulp stocks up in December -Finnish paper.</title>
<headline>Swedish pulp stocks up in December -Finnish paper.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1997-01-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish pulp producers' Norscan pulp inventories rose by 50,000 tonnes in December, Finnish daily Kauppalehti reported on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The increase corresponds to six days' output and the stocks are now equal to 26 days, it said.</p>
<p>Finnish producers' stocks fell some 7,000 tonnes and Norwegians' stocks also fell slightly, it said.</p>
<p>North American producers' data was not yet available.</p>
<p>-- Helsinki Newsroom +358-9-680 50 242</p>
